+**Step 1 (fixtures, no behaviour change).** The 733-check baseline did not reproduce from a clean clone: `arty_rows.json` was missing, `se_sample_rows.json` had anonymised DOBs that disagreed with the tests, and the anonymised roster disagreed with identity values hard-coded in `probe_se_import.js`. Replaced the real/pseudonymised child with a fully synthetic one (Nic / Nicholas Marlowe, SE # 7000001, made-up DOB), renamed fixtures to `nic_rows.json` / `nic_roster.json`, removed `john_rows.json`, added `make_sample_xlsx.py` and `run_all_tests.sh`. Logo hash unchanged. (A first, blunt search-and-replace also rewrote the GitHub username inside the QT sync URLs; caught by diffing `index.html` and reverted before commit.) Git history still holds the old fixtures (known-bugs #16).
+
+**Step 2 (v2.13.1: #29, #30, #28).** Tests first (`probe_v213.js`, 35 checks, 28 red against the old app for the right reasons; one test-fixture slip of mine fixed first). Duplicate radios stacked with bold names and outcomes; speed emoji; wording swept across the SE review/summary/card, sync and upload notes, Keep/Hide/Remove help and the Remove confirmation. 19 older assertions on the old wording were updated deliberately (list in the commit). Title bumped to v2.13.1. **Layout is unverified until the coach tests it** (jsdom has no layout): `user_test_script_v2.13.md` Part 1.
+
+**Testing:** 768 checks (733 + 35), 0 failures. Apps Script unchanged (2.2.4-b5).
+
+**v2.13.2 (fix after coach UAT of v2.13.1).** The coach's screenshots showed each swimmer's Probable duplicates nested inside the previous one, text squeezed into a narrow column. Root cause: my #29 replacement of the radio block dropped the closing `</div>` of the new choices container, so every following duplicate and swimmer opened inside the previous one. jsdom silently repairs unclosed tags, and my first tests only checked that radios shared a parent, so it passed. Reproduced first with structural tests (rows are siblings; `<div>`/`</div>` balanced across the duplicate, two-candidate and conflict variants; 5 red), then fixed. Standing rule added: any change to rendered HTML gets an explicit balanced-tags / sibling-structure check, not just a content check. Title bumped to v2.13.2. 776 checks (768 + 8), 0 failures; the coach's remaining Part 1 steps are still to be run.
+
+**v2.13.3 (wording, from coach UAT of v2.13.2).** All v2.13.2 Part 1-4 steps passed. Coach observation: "on file" in the review reads as "in the imported file"; and "your best time" reads as the coach's. Suggestion agreed ("in the dashboard"; "the swimmer's"). Tests first (`probe_v213.js` +31 checks, 22 red), then ~25 exact-match replacements; residue checked by grep. Legacy assertions pinning the old phrases updated deliberately in 6 probes. Count line is now "Swimming results in the dashboard". Title v2.13.3. **807 checks, 0 failures**; logo unchanged; Apps Script unchanged. Process notes: running the full suite twice in one command exceeded the 300 s tool limit, and a `pkill -f` pattern matched its own shell; the suite is now run once, in the background, and polled. `run_all_tests.sh` takes roughly 4-5 minutes.
+
+**v2.13.3 UAT:** all 19 steps passed. Decisions for the rest of v2.13: ship #20 as v2.13.4 and the Swimmers tab as v2.13.5 (separately); no Hide/Show toggle on the Swimmers tab until the merge tool; a "possible duplicate" flag on same normalised name regardless of DOB; no "latest result date" column; the tab is labelled "👥 Swimmers".
+
+**v2.13.4 (#20, filter footer counts).** Tests first (`probe_v2134.js`, 29 checks; 19 red: every filter-removed swimmer was missing from the accounting). One `filterMisses` helper (Gender, Age Group, Squad, name search, in the filter bar's order) now drives both the visible list and a new footer group "N not matching the Gender / Age Group / Squad / name filters", each swimmer listed with the filters that removed them; precedence hidden > Former > filter > the existing no-rows diagnosis, so nobody is counted twice. Search text and names are escaped. Title v2.13.4; the two title assertions were loosened to `v2.13.\d+` so they stop needing an edit each release. **836 checks, 0 failures**; logo and Apps Script unchanged. Layout of the footer on a real screen is unverified until the coach tests (`user_test_script_v2.13.4.md`).
+
+**v2.13.4 UAT:** counts and categories passed; coach found the wording misleading ("John Smith - Gender (Girls)" reads as a fact about John, when it means the filter that excluded him). Agreed redesign, shipped alone as v2.13.5: the heading names the active filters once ("N not matching the active filters (Gender: Girls · Squad: Junior)") and each row shows what the swimmer IS for the filters they failed ("John Smith - Boys", "Carl Beta - Boys, Senior", "Fay Eps - No squad", name doesn't contain "zzz"). Tests first: 17 red, then `filterMisses` returns the swimmer's own value and `buildFooterNote` takes the active-filter text. Added checks that no row uses the old "Filter (value)" style or repeats the asked-for value, and that the heading lists exactly the active filters in filter-bar order. Which swimmers are shown/listed is unchanged. **842 checks, 0 failures**; logo and Apps Script unchanged. Lesson: when text names a filter and a person on one line, say which is which; the first wording was mine and I tested the counts, not how the sentence reads.
