+match "Expected", tell me the step number and what you saw (a screenshot helps).
+
+## Part 0
+- [ ] **0.1** Tab title says **Coach Dashboard v2.13.3** (hard refresh if it still says v2.13.2).
+- [ ] **0.2** Download a fresh backup first (Manage Data > Full Backup & Restore).
+
+## Part 1 - "on file" is gone from the SE review
+Run an SE import that shows Time conflicts, Probable duplicates and (if you can) a "Nothing to import" screen. Read every line.
+- [ ] **1.1** Nowhere does it say "on file" or "on-file". Where the existing data is meant it says **in the dashboard** or **dashboard** (or just describes the entry).
+- [ ] **1.2** Time conflict row: "200 Free (SC), 5 Jul 2026: in the dashboard **3:13.52** vs SE report **3:11.36**".
+- [ ] **1.3** Orange notes read "The SE time is 2.16s faster ⚡ than the swimmer's best in the dashboard (3:13.52), so Keep existing leaves the swimmer's best at 3:13.52." and "... 0.38s slower 🐢 than the swimmer's best in the dashboard (30.37). Using the SE report would make the swimmer's best time in the dashboard slower."
+- [ ] **1.4** A repeated time reads "The dashboard time 3:13.52 is also recorded on 29 Nov 2025."
+- [ ] **1.5** Probable duplicates: "...in the dashboard dated 1 Jul 2025, SE report dated 22 Feb 2025"; with two same-time entries "in the dashboard with this time on 1 Jul 2025 and 28 Sep 2025", "2 entries in the dashboard have this time...", and Merge says "replace all 2 dashboard entries with the one SE swim (removes 1 duplicate)".
+- [ ] **1.6** The grey list "swimming result time(s) in the dashboard appear on more than one date - possible duplicates" (if shown).
+- [ ] **1.7** Bottom note: "Nothing to import. 15 result(s) already match what's in the dashboard." and, when something will happen, "replace N time(s) in the dashboard with the SE report's", "remove N repeated dashboard result(s)".
+
+## Part 2 - "your" is gone where it meant the swimmer
+- [ ] **2.1** The Time conflicts explainer says "the SE report and the dashboard both have a swim on the same date...", "'Keep existing' leaves the dashboard time...", "'Use SE report' replaces the dashboard time...". 
+- [ ] **2.2** The Probable duplicates explainer says "leaves the existing record untouched".
+- [ ] **2.3** In the auto-matched box (when a nickname differs): "the name in the dashboard is never changed".
+- [ ] **2.4** Phrases that address YOU are still natural: "Tick it only if you're confident...", "Choose your club's Short Course and/or Long Course export(s)".
