+# Coach Dashboard - v2.13.2 test script (v2.13.1 had a layout bug in Part 1, fixed here) (review-screen polish: #29, #30, #28)
+
+Three small changes to the SE import review screen and the wording around it. My automated tests prove the
+text and structure, but **not how it looks on a real screen**, so the layout steps (Part 1) are the ones where
+your eyes matter. If anything does not match "Expected", stop and tell me the step number (a screenshot helps).
+
+## Part 0 - Before you start
+- [ ] **0.1** Tab title says **Coach Dashboard v2.13.2** (if it still says v2.12.11 or v2.13.1 your browser has the old file: hard refresh).
+- [ ] **0.2** Download a fresh backup (Manage Data > Full Backup & Restore). The Apps Script is unchanged (build 2.2.4-b5).
+
+## Part 1 - Probable duplicates layout (#29) - check on desktop AND a phone-width window
+Use your SE import with a swimmer who shows under "Probable duplicates" (e.g. a single same-time entry, and the two-entry case such as Nicole).
+- [ ] **1.0** (regression from the first v2.13.1 test) With several swimmers in Probable duplicates, each swimmer has **its own separate box**, one under the other: nothing is nested inside the previous swimmer's box and the text is not squeezed into a narrow column.
+- [ ] **1.1** Each choice is on **its own row**, one under the other (not side by side).
+- [ ] **1.2** Each row starts with a **bold name** followed by a dash and what it does, e.g.
+  - **Skip** - keep the existing entry and don't import the SE swim
+  - **Replace** - move the 1 Jul 2025 entry to the SE date 22 Feb 2025
+  - **Import separately** - keep the existing entry and also add the SE swim dated 22 Feb 2025 as its own result
+- [ ] **1.3** With two same-time entries on file you see: Skip, **Replace** (first date), **Replace** (second date), **Merge** (says it replaces all N entries with the one SE swim and how many duplicates it removes), Import separately.
+- [ ] **1.4** The bold names match the buttons above them: **Skip for all / Replace for all / Import separately for all** (Merge has no "for all" button, as before).
+- [ ] **1.5** Clicking a choice still works: the note at the bottom updates ("add N new swimming result(s)", "update N existing swimming result(s)") and the list does not jump back to the top.
+- [ ] **1.6** On a phone-width window long descriptions wrap onto the next line inside their row and nothing runs off the screen.
+
+## Part 2 - Speed emoji on the conflict note (#30)
+- [ ] **2.1** On a Time conflict where the SE time is **faster** than your best, the orange note reads "...2.16s faster ⚡ than the best on file (...)".
+- [ ] **2.2** Where the SE time is **slower** (e.g. Jager), it reads "...0.38s slower 🐢 than the best on file (...)" and, if it applies, still ends with "Using the SE report would make your best time on file slower."
+- [ ] **2.3** No emoji appears on rows where there is no time difference note.
+
+## Part 3 - Wording: "swimming results" (#28)
+Look for the words **PB result(s)**, **PB record(s)** or **PB(s)** anywhere below. There should be none; "PB" is kept only where it means a personal best (e.g. Hot Right Now, County/Regional "PB Time").
+- [ ] **3.1** SE import review: "N new swimming result(s) will be added", "N existing swimming result(s) will be updated", and the sentence under Suggested matches ("Ticking a box imports swimming results...").
+- [ ] **3.2** SE import summary after Apply: "N new swimming result(s) added", "... swimming result(s) updated to the SE report's time", "... kept as recorded", "... updated with the SE report's real date". The "Swimming results on file: before -> after" line still balances.
+- [ ] **3.3** Google Sheet sync with Remove selected: the dropdown reads "Remove (delete swimmer and all their swimming results)", the help text below it says "swimming results", and the confirmation lists "Name (3 swimming results)" and "ALL n of their swimming results". Press Cancel: nothing changes.
+- [ ] **3.4** If a sync or upload-merge shows an SE note, it says "SE-confirmed swimming result(s) differed..." / "...swimming result(s)... were not re-added".
+- [ ] **3.5** Manage Data > SE PB Report Import card says "adds or reconciles swimming results" (the card's own title keeps the report's name, "SE PB Report").
+
+## Part 4 - Nothing else broke
+- [ ] **4.1** Overview, County QT and Regional QT tabs load as before; Add/Edit Swimmer saves (the form still says "Personal Bests" / "Add PB entry": that wording moves with the later `pbs` rename).
+- [ ] **4.2** A full SE import still balances and Backup downloads.
